    {
      "id": 83560,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-12-04T15:31:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I'm seeing a turn where Expat plays an ammo card, then Aims, knowing she has unload for next turn, then Greatest Legacy throws another power her way, and Adept goes crazy giving her more card plays for ammo or to finish out her Arsenal, and a power use (or two depending on how many cards are there to play), then on Expat's turn she unloads with multiple ammo in play and a +4 to damage dealt. &nbsp;The absurd amounts of damage she is capable of now. . .</p><p>I understand why they aren't popular, but I find them to be two of the most reliable heroes, and often Expat carries a team through the first few rounds when others are trying to set up still. &nbsp;Fixer I just love. &nbsp;So much he can do to set up his team to crush a villain. &nbsp;I love support characters, and the more subtle the better. &nbsp;Fixer is a melee support, which is something I love. &nbsp;(I once RP'd a Warrior who specialized in disarming, tripping and grappling. &nbsp;He did almost no damage, but was amazing)</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:06:40.899Z",
